  "name": "Child and Adolescent Development",
  "description": "This course provides an overview of the typical physical, social, emotional, moral, and cognitive developmental changes occurring during middle childhood and adolescence. Students explore major theoretical concepts and strategies of interaction with individuals in this age group. Course activity focuses on typical and atypical aspects of development the contexts and social spheres that shape middle childhood and adolescence as well as transitions from middle childhood to adolescence.",
